<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A drone sprays a shamba, flying in a straight line from <m>A({-5},\,{-2},\,{1})</m> to <m>B({5},\,{5},\,{-2})</m>. Coordinates are in metres, measured from a corner post O.</p><p>(a) Write the position vector of B, <m>\mathbf{b} = \overrightarrow{OB}</m>.</p><div><m>\mathbf{b} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Write the vector <m>\overrightarrow{AB}</m>.</p><div><m>\overrightarrow{AB} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The position vector of B is the journey from the origin to B, so it lists B's coordinates: <m>\mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 5 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>\overrightarrow{AB} = \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a}</m>, end minus start: <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} 5 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{array}\right)} - {\left(\begin{array}{c} -5 \\ -2 \\ 1 \end{array}\right)} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 10 \\ 7 \\ -3 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} 5 \\ 5 \\ -2 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} 10 \\ 7 \\ -3 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>